course: dictionary
lesson: 2709
title: Digraphs: two letters, one sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A digraph is two letters that work together to make one sound. In «ship», the s and h make one hushing sound, «sh», not two separate sounds. Say it slowly and listen for the one sound.
explain: Digraphs can come at the start, middle or end of a word. Consonant digraphs, such as «ch» in «chip» and «th» in «thin», use consonant letters. Vowel digraphs, such as «ee» in «see» and «ai» in «rain», use vowel letters.
explain: A trigraph is three letters that make one sound, such as «igh» in «night». When you read, look for these letter teams first, then sound each team out as one unit.
fact: A digraph is two letters making one sound.
fact: «sh» in «ship», «ch» in «chip» and «th» in «thin» are consonant digraphs.
fact: «ee» in «see» and «ai» in «rain» are vowel digraphs.
fact: A trigraph is three letters making one sound, like «igh» in «night» or «air» in «air».
fact: In a split digraph such as a-e, e-e, i-e, o-e or u-e, the silent e makes the vowel say its name: hop becomes hope, and kit becomes kite.
exercise: Which two letters make one sound in «ship»? | ip | *sh | si | hi
exercise: Which word has a vowel digraph? | tap | hop | cub | *rain
exercise: In «night», how many letters make the one sound igh? | Two | Four | *Three
test: Which word shows a split digraph? | cup | cub | cut | *cube
test: Which word starts with a consonant digraph? | eel | owl | *thin | ask
exam: In «chip», what kind of digraph is ch? | Split digraph | Vowel digraph | *Consonant digraph | Trigraph
